PROJECT PURPOSE
---------------
This project implements an end-to-end customer churn analytics system suitable
for an Associate Data / Data Science role.

The goal is to demonstrate:
- Clean Python ETL
- Feature engineering
- Machine learning modeling
- MySQL as an analytics database
- Power BI for business consumption

ARCHITECTURE (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
-----------------------------
Raw CSV
  → Python ingestion
  → MySQL table: customers_raw
  → Python feature engineering
  → MySQL table: feature_store
  → Python ML model (XGBoost / RandomForest)
  → MySQL table: model_predictions
  → Power BI dashboard

BOUNDARIES (VERY IMPORTANT)
---------------------------
- NO modeling inside Power BI
- NO business logic inside notebooks
- NO direct CSV consumption by Power BI
- MySQL is the single source of truth
- All ML logic lives in Python scripts

FILE RESPONSIBILITIES
---------------------
config.py     → constants only (DB names, table names, paths)
utils.py      → DB engine + helpers (NO business logic)
ingest.py     → CSV → customers_raw
features.py   → customers_raw → feature_store
train.py      → train & evaluate model, save to disk
registry.py   → verify artifacts, register unapproved benchmark models
score.py      → explicit benchmark scoring, write model_predictions
run_pipeline.py → orchestrate steps in order

QUALITY RULES
-------------
- Code must be deterministic and re-runnable
- Explicit validation preferred over silent failure
- Clear variable and function names
- Avoid clever abstractions
- Readability > performance

ML REQUIREMENTS
---------------
- Use train/validation split
- Use PR-AUC (average precision) as primary metric; also report ROC-AUC
- Report precision/recall
- Handle class imbalance explicitly
- Save model artifact

DATABASE RULES
--------------
- Explicit schemas
- Primary keys required
- No SELECT *
- No JSON blobs

POWER BI RULES
--------------
- Connect ONLY to model_predictions table; distinguish benchmark scores from production
- KPIs must be business-oriented
- Avoid excessive calculated columns

COPILOT USAGE
-------------
- Copilot is used for boilerplate and speed
- Architecture and logic decisions are human-driven
- Reject outputs that violate this document

If any generated code violates these rules, it must be rewritten.
